* Create virtualenv for python 3.10
* Activate the virtualenv
- go to cmd/terminal
    * pip install -r requirements.txt
- create .env file inside src/core/.env
- put settings parameters for project environment
* create postgres db
    - go to cmd/terminal
        > sudo su postgres psql
        > create database test_db;
        > create user test_user with password 'mu123456';
        > GRANT ALL PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE test_db TO test_user;
        > \q
        > exit
* go to src/core/.env end edit accordingly
* Auto generate Alembic revisions for the models present
        - go to cmd/terminal
        > alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Adding User .."  ** put your comments
        > alembic upgrade head

